      { q: "A historian finds that a Persian chronicle and a Sikh work describe the same battle differently. What should she do?", options: ["Accept the Persian one because it is older", "Accept the Sikh one because it is local", "Compare both with other evidence such as letters or monuments", "Leave the battle out of her book"], answer: 2, explain: "When sources disagree, a historian weighs each author's position and checks it against independent evidence.", level: 3 }
